    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0265" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72Su/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Liaison Officer with the Supreme War
                        Council</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Frazier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-26T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 1.41 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Referring to my telegram No. 23, March 18, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d112-f1"/>
                    Signor Gallavresi of the Italian Legation in Berne informed
                    me today that article 15 of the secret treaty between Great Britain and Italy
                    had been imperfectly and inaccurately revealed by the Russian
                        Maximalists.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d112-f2"/> The actual sense of the article
                    was that Great Britain had agreed, in case the Pope proposed peace negotiations
                    with any intention of reviving the question of temporal power, not to accept his
                    intervention without consulting Italy. Gallavresi could not
                    tell me to what extent this article had been modified at the meeting on the 16th
                    instant in London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frazier</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
